I think the non-foo effect should be limited, perhaps non-existent. There
are other artifact weapons that are general use. This gives more
diversity. Of course, the foo-effect should be very good, or one will
never take the trouble of carrying the weapon with him.

> Er I thought you wanted to make the banes *better*? :)

The corpse disappearing and leaving no other remains makes it worse, but
that is easily compensated by the suggested instant-kill ability of the
Banes. Note that they only work for a *very* small class of monsters, and
that you'd have to carry them with you all the time, without much use the
rest of the time.

> Not especially but I'm one of those people who
> is against a lot more insta-kills.  A damage multiplier
> seems like something close to the same effect with
> more control, should it be x3, x4 ?...

I'm a balance freak, but I don't think the Banes having an instant kill
capability would be too good. It's just one class of monsters they're
effective against, and as said, you'd have to be carrying them all the
time.

>>>> [Giantslayer]

>> Maybe it could automatically slice thrown boulders
>> into rocks if they were thrown at you.

> Hm! And perhaps at all other times too as in my other post.

No... Just the boulders thrown. Otherwise it wouldn't be related to giants
anymore.

> One area might be various powers that can only be gained through
> polymorph (flying and wall-passing spring to mind), being moved
> to artifact weapons (or/and spells).  The Phase Cloak, an artifact
> cloak of displacement that lets you pass through walls for a
> short time after an #invoke.

I'd like those kinds of artifacts. Note, however, that having a lot of
"small" artifacts (artifacts conferring only a very limited ability), will
mean that the chance of a good artifact being generated decreases rapidly.
If you get, say, three or four of those, your chances of getting a few
more from your god or from wishing decrease. Whether that is a bad thing
is debatable, of course. Games would certainly become more varied this
way.

> I think that sort of thing should start with the idea of completely
> shutting off the ability to wish for the quest artifacts of other
> classes.

I've propagated that in the past, but the Dev Team dealt with this by
limiting the number and alignment of quest artifacts you can wish for.

